From: openEuler RISC-V Maintainers <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] Preserve interior separators and ASCII alphanumeric contracts

Exact-head target CI ran all 13 original tests and found three failures. The
first camelcase substitution deletes the letters around an interior separator
(foo-bar becomes foar); pascalcase inherits this error. Strip only leading
separators, retaining the existing interior separator-to-uppercase pass and
the original leading underscore/dot expectations. In alphanumcase, \W retains
underscores despite the documented 0-9, a-z and A-Z contract. Use that explicit
ASCII complement while retaining Patch0's str(input) normalization.

Source: repository-authored against official release-associated MIT commit
be60b723753d4796983729d49ef825826e0f882d, applied after Patch0. The newer official
57aae96649f5cf7fc98e50b1d62479456d492715 was reviewed, but its broader camelcase
rewrite and Unicode isalnum behavior do not preserve this stable contract.
Upstream status: local packaging fix, not submitted upstream.
Removal: drop when a verified stable upstream release preserves these contracts
and passes its complete unchanged original/default suite without this patch.
No original tests, coverage commands or installed acceptance are changed.

--- a/stringcase.py
+++ b/stringcase.py
@@ -19 +19 @@ def camelcase(string):
-    string = re.sub(r"\w[\s\W]+\w", '', str(string))
+    string = re.sub(r'^[\-_\.]+', '', str(string))
@@ -245,3 +245,3 @@ def alphanumcase(string):
     """
     # return filter(str.isalnum, str(string))
-    return re.sub("\W+", "", str(string))
+    return re.sub(r'[^0-9a-zA-Z]+', "", str(string))
